{
 "format": {
  "name": "tessel",
  "version": 1
 },
 "meta": {
  "title": "Receipt email",
  "description": "An email, 600 wide (never a post): the Email frame is the email's card and each child is a section, top to bottom. Restyle it in the brand with set_tokens (color.brand for the button and pill, color.ink, color.paper the card, color.page around it, color.night the footer; font.heading, font.body), put the business's name in Logo and FooterName (or replace Logo with the logo as an image layer named for its alt text) and its own words everywhere. {{field}} words are filled for each person; keep them. A layer named link:<address> links: rename it to the real address. Save it as a template with email_design_save, declaring its fields. A payment receipt (transactional; the payment hook fills it). Fields: amount, invoice_number, paid_on, balance (default \"Nothing\"), and lines (a list, optional: the repeat:lines rows show what was paid for, each row's {{item}}, {{qty}} and {{amount}}; ifnot:lines draws when there are none). Subject \"Payment received, thank you\"; preheader \"We received {{amount}} for invoice {{invoice_number}}.\""
 },
